<Item XName="Text" Type="Param">
<DataEntry>In this design the Etheta, Ephi parameters of the ArrayAnt model are set to represent two in-phase equal strength polarization components. The circuitry behind the antenna (PhaseShifter, Attenuator, Combiner/Splitter) is responsible for implementing the desired polarization.&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;Since NumAntennasPerLocation = 2, Etheta and Ephi are 2x1 vectors and there will be 2*8*8=128 signals at the output of the ArrayAnt model. The odd ordered ones (1, 3, 5, ...) represent the signals from the Etheta polarized antenna and the even ordered ones (2, 4, 6, ...) represent the signals from the Ephi polarized antenna. The PhaseShifter applies the desired phase to all the even ordered signals and the Attenuator applies the appropriate attenuation to the odd or even ordered signals to achieve the desired polarization. The variables PhaseShift and CustomWindow used in the PhaseShifter and Attenuator are defined in the design equations page. The first Combiner/Splitter after/before the antenna combines/splits the signals for the two antennas at the same array location.&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;Beam steering happens after the first combiner/splitter.</DataEntry>
<TextParam><T>Bool</T><D>1</D></TextParam></Item></Item>
