<Item XName="Text" Type="Param">
<DataEntry>This configuration is similar to Configuration 1 but the order of beam steering and polarization control is switched.&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;The combiner/splitter after/before the beam steering PhaseShifter needs to combine/split the signals from/to all the Etheta and Ephi antennas. This is done using the Custom Mode and an ElementMap using alternating 1 and 2 values. In the Rx mode where the ArraySplit acts as a combiner this custom ElementMap means that there are only 2 combiners since the values in the ElementMap array are only 1 and 2. The indices of the 1 and 2 elements specify the indices of the signals at the output of the Beam steering PhaseShifter that will be routed to combiner 1 and combiner 2. Since the 1 values are in the odd ordered elements of ElementMap, all the odd ordered signals at the output of the beam steering PhaseShifter (the signals from the Etheta antennas) will be router to combiner 1. Similarly all the signals from the Ephi antennas will be routed to combiner 2.&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;After this first combiner we are left with only two signals. The first one represents the combined voltage of all Etheta antennas and the second one represents the combined voltage of all Ephi antennas. The circuitry that follows (PhaseShifter, Attenuator, Combiner) implements the polarization controls the same way it is done in Design 1.</DataEntry>
<TextParam><T>Bool</T><D>1</D></TextParam></Item></Item>
